ET /v2/conflicts` and compare it **row-by-row** against
> the four individually enumerated rows of the Gate 2D
> approved baseline (pin
> `9284f5efee47cd87b2c5639e9dfe50e6fb7e908a`, `BASELINE.md` §
> "Complete conflict set"), reproduced verbatim in §4.4.1
> below. The census passes **only** on an exact match: same
> four rows, same ids, same timestamps, same occurrence ids,
> same field values. **ANY addition, deletion, or field
> change — in count, id, timestamp, occurrence, or any
> field — is a STOP before any mutation.** On such a STOP,
> the complete new census is pinned and returned to Rowan
> for a specific baseline ruling; **only a separately
> reviewed replacement baseline may be used** for a later
> attempt. No executor judgment call, and no "matching
> signature" exemption for a fifth or changed row, can clear
> a changed set.

